+=== 2D shape outline
+
+In addition to bounding box, OSI supports defining a more precise 2D shape outline (https://opensimulationinterface.github.io/osi-antora-generator/asamosi/latest/gen/structosi3_1_1BaseMoving.html#a584e39108fe12db4933390975a172c63[base_polygon]) for entities, by specifying a set 2D (x,y) points in the entity's local coordinate system.
+
+.Outline example
+image::outlines_car.jpg[]
+
+This is, for example, useful for NCAP scenarios where a more precise collision detection is required, see https://www.euroncap.com/media/95012/ca-004-data-acquisition-and-assessment-criteria-calculation-v11.pdf#page=9[Euro NCAP Data Acquisition
+And Assessment Criteria Calculation]
+
+Currently OpenSCENARIO XML does not support defining 2D shape outlines in a standardized way. However, the Property elements of https://publications.pages.asam.net/standards/ASAM_OpenSCENARIO/ASAM_OpenSCENARIO_XML/latest/generated/content/EntityObject.html[EntityObject] (Vehicle, Pedestrian, MiscObject) can be utilized for this purpose. From version 2.58.0 esmini supports reading 2D shape outlines defined as property with name `outline` and value on the format: `x0,y0;x1,y1;x2,y2,...`. Example of four points:
+
+[source,xml]
+----
+<Property name="outline" value="-1.5,-2.0;1.5,-2.0;1.5,2.0;-1.5,2.0"/>
+----
+
+resulting in a rectangular shape outline 3x4 meters, centered at the reference point of the entity.
+
+A full example, shown in image above, can be found in the esmini demo vehicle catalog https://github.com/esmini/esmini/blob/cf7387b5071870128959712739002fa1c685c0e1/resources/xosc/Catalogs/Vehicles/VehicleCatalog.xosc#L53-L87[VehicleCatalog.xosc/car_white_with_outline]. Points calculated using this https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Bc6T6FH1yP6PzW9zeZdmwzWGdaDU6vs17frhorkltHI/edit?usp=sharing[Google sheet] (`File -> Make a copy` to edit your own values).
+
+The test scenario https://github.com/esmini/esmini/blob/dev/EnvironmentSimulator/Unittest/xosc/shape_outlines.xosc[shape_outlines.xosc] includes a few more examples for various entity types. Video clip https://youtu.be/YZX2P4F5Rj8[here].
+
+.Further outline examples
+image::outlines.jpg[]
+
+Note that the outline is independent and does not have to exactly match the 3D model of the entity.
+
+The visualization of the 2D shape outlines is activated by default. It can be disabled by option `--hide_obj_outline` and toggled on/off in `esmini` and `replayer` with `;` (shift + comma).
+
